Wed Oct  7 07:40:27 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to version 2.0.0 (major):
  * Structured tool outputs with output schemas, gated on MCP
    protocol 2026-07-28 or newer; older, unknown or version-less
    clients keep the legacy text without output schemas or
    structured content
  * Compound tools with updated output schemas are withheld from
    older clients; no tool is renamed or removed
  * Modern clients get compact DTOs instead of raw REST objects:
    release, ref, tag, commit, directory, gist, issue, search and
    Actions results omit API and hypermedia URLs while keeping
    browser links and identifiers; search_repositories with
    minimal_output=false returns curated details, not the full
    GitHub API object
  * find_duplicate page and perPage now accept 0, forwarded for
    the GitHub API default
  * See upstream's release notes for the full list
- Refresh the vendored Go modules for the new source (same module
  versions; segmentio/encoding becomes direct): re-derived over
  the new tree, still only MIT, BSD-3-Clause and Apache-2.0, no
  copyleft; the crossed range and release notes name no CVE
- go.mod still requires go 1.26.8, so the golang(API) >= 1.26.8
  floor stands

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sun Oct  4 06:59:42 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to version 1.14.0:
  * Looking up a pending pull request review now works when the
    authenticated actor is a Copilot bot
  * See upstream's release notes for the full list
- Refresh the vendored Go modules: go-github v89 -> v92, the MCP Go
  SDK 1.7.0 -> 1.8.0, shurcooL/githubv4 and graphql, and
  golang.org/x net, oauth2, sync, sys and text. Re-derived over the
  new tree: still only MIT, BSD-3-Clause and Apache-2.0, no copyleft.
  * The MCP Go SDK 1.8.0 caps JSON nesting, SSE event size and the
    stdio frame length, bounds OAuth client registration, and fixes
    session leaks and a teardown deadlock; upstream names no CVE
  * This build does not compile the ui/ TypeScript tree, so the
    release's TypeScript 7 and React 19 work does not apply to it;
    the MCP Apps SDK v2 pull request only rewrites pointer
    construction in the server (github.Ptr -> new) with no behaviour
    change
- go.mod now requires go 1.26.8, so BuildRequires on golang(API) moves
  from >= 1.26 to >= 1.26.8; the old floor admitted 1.26.0, which is
  older than the directive and cannot build the module

