Fri Oct  2 09:43:21 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to version 1.13.0:
  * New granular tools hide and unhide issue comments, pull request
    review comments and pull request reviews, so a minimized item
    is restored by a dedicated call instead of a consolidated
    write: hide_issue_comment and unhide_issue_comment in the
    issues toolset, hide_pull_request_review_comment,
    unhide_pull_request_review_comment, hide_pull_request_review
    and unhide_pull_request_review in the pull requests toolset.
  * MCP Apps is no longer behind the remote_mcp_ui_apps feature
    flag: _meta.ui is now emitted, and the form-backed write tools
    defer to a form this build cannot serve, since the bundled UI
    is not built. Pass --features mcp_apps_disable_form_deferral to
    keep them executing directly.
  * The stdio transport now sends a versioned GitHub API user agent
    even before the handshake, warning on stderr if none resolves.
  * See upstream's release notes for the full list.
- Vendored Go modules are unchanged (go.mod/go.sum identical to
  1.12.2), so the licence audit stands: the 32 modules linked into
  both binaries are MIT, BSD-3-Clause or Apache-2.0, no copyleft.

